EXECUTIVE WORKING PRODUCT | INTERNAL | NON-FINAL

UNGA81 GENERAL DEBATE | 23 SEPTEMBER 2026
Coverage: 39 supplied country speeches

EXECUTIVE TAKEAWAY
Statements combined calls to strengthen multilateral institutions with differ=
ent approaches to reform. Botswana sought protection of operational programs,=
 while Spain called for abolition of the Security Council veto. On AI, Argent=
ina opposed preemptive regulation, while the Czech Republic and Italy sought =
common international rules.

SELECTED SPECIFIC REQUESTS
- Organized crime. Ecuador proposed a financial-tracing mechanism, a permanen=
t information-sharing platform, and inclusion of organized crime in UN80 conf=
lict-prevention priorities.
- Haiti. The Dominican Republic sought renewal and resourcing of the Gang Sup=
pression Force before the 30 September expiry stated in its speech.
- Public health. Palau requested a WHO review of nicotine as a psychotropic s=
ubstance.

CROSS-SPEECH ISSUE PATTERNS
Issue codes are non-exclusive. UN reform & representation: 32/39; human right=
s/health/social: 30/39; other peace & security: 28/39.

